=== TOON Format ===
mcptoon supports standard TOON (Token-Oriented Object Notation) as defined
by the toon-format/toon open spec (https://github.com/toon-format/toon).
The SLIM format (name|param:type*) is an mcptoon-specific innovation.

TOON encoder/decoder is vendored from python-toon v0.1.1
(https://github.com/xaviviro/python-toon), Copyright (c) Xavi Vinaixa,
licensed under the MIT License. See src/mcptoon/toon_vendored.py for
the full copyright notice and license terms.

If you implement TOON encoding in a derivative work, please reference
the standard TOON spec. If you implement SLIM format, please:
  1. Attribute the original design to mcptoon
  2. Include a reference to https://github.com/activeing123/mcptoon
  3. Include this NOTICE file

=== Third-Party Acknowledgments ===
This project is inspired by the Model Context Protocol (MCP) specification
by Anthropic (https://modelcontextprotocol.io/). mcptoon is an independent
implementation and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic.

=== OpenAPI adapter — design inspiration ===
The `mcptoon openapi` adapter (src/mcptoon/openapi.py) is an independent,
stdlib-only implementation. Its design conventions — operation naming from
operationId, path-item parameter inheritance, Optional[T] union collapsing,
and request-body content negotiation — follow the approach popularised by
knowsuchagency/mcp2cli (https://github.com/knowsuchagency/mcp2cli),
Copyright (c) 2026 Stephan Fitzpatrick, licensed under the MIT License.
No mcp2cli source code is included; this notice records the design lineage.

=== oh-my-context (derived work) ===
oh-my-context is derived from mcptoon 0.8.33 by activeing123
(https://github.com/activeing123/mcptoon), licensed under the Apache License
2.0. It ships in oh-my-context-mod (https://github.com/prv-ctech/claude-code-linux,
mods/oh-my-context-mod). The text above is mcptoon's own NOTICE, kept verbatim;
its "src/mcptoon/..." paths are upstream's. Modifications made by
oh-my-context-mod (Apache License 2.0, section 4), 2026-10-30, are listed
below. Each changed file has a "Modified by oh-my-context-mod" header and each
functional change an "oh-my-context-mod:" comment.

Renamed in every file of oh_my_context/:
  the package mcptoon -> oh_my_context; the program and CLI name mcptoon ->
  oh-my-context; the gateway's own tools mcptoon_<name> -> <name> (call,
  inspect, manifest, resolve_skills, servers, health, usage, skills, retrieve,
  kb_search, kb_index, session); environment variables MCPTOON_* -> OMC_*;
  default folders and files ~/.mcptoon -> the plugin's data folder (OMC_HOME);
  internal identifiers containing mcptoon -> omc; links to the upstream
  repository -> this repository.

Only what the plugin runs is kept: the CLI commands `--version`, `serve`
(stdio), `hint` and `skills index <dir>`, the gateway's MCP tools and what they
reach. Not included (removed, or never vendored): mcptoon's own agent skill
(skill/SKILL.md), python-toon (_toon/, toon_vendored.py) and the TOON/SLIM output
formats, and the modules bake.py, bench.py, demo.py, demo_server.py, discover.py,
docs.py, errors.py, exec_sandbox.py, footer.py, graphql.py, health.py,
installer.py, manifest.py, mcp_extras.py, mode.py, oauth.py, openapi.py,
output.py, packs.py, packs.json, bench_tokens.py, report.py, savings.py,
sync.py, update.py, upgrade.py, watch.py and welcome.py. Every other CLI command
(sync, quickstart, init, restore, off, install, uninstall, add, remove, list,
manifest, inspect, search, select, call, exec, usage, status, stats, activity,
report, savings, mode, credit, statusline, docs, kb, openapi, graphql, auth,
resources, prompts, complete, bake, session, retrieve, footer-facts, toggle,
policy, discover, import, doctor, update, upgrade, completion, health, plugin,
skills <other actions>, bench, config, help, demo, demo-server and the
natural-language fallback) is removed with its handler; an unknown command
prints a usage line and exits 2. Removed with them: the footer, presence line,
welcome, star hint and self-heal; serve's HTTP, background and autostart modes;
the per-tool compression policies, toggles and all settings except `exposure`
and `compress`; the skills LLM route, skills.sh search, sync, doctor, version
gate, gloss and usage counts; the kb URL fetch; the activity ledger; tiktoken
token counting; and the OMC_* environment overrides other than OMC_HOME,
OMC_CONFIG_FILE and OMC_MOD_PYTHONPATH. Nothing left reaches the network except
the HTTP MCP servers the gateway routes.

  oh_my_context/cli.py           only --version, serve, hint and skills index
                                 <dir> (see above).
  oh_my_context/hint.py          added: `oh-my-context hint`, read-only skill and
                                 tool hints for a prompt.
  oh_my_context/config.py        reads only OMC_CONFIG_FILE (written by
                                 hooks/sync.js; no project-local, TOML or
                                 OMC_SERVERS config); servers with "cwd_only"
                                 load only in that project, and servers with
                                 "cwd_except" not in the projects it lists; an
                                 unreadable config's backup is created owner-only
                                 (0600) and never overwritten; settings are
                                 `exposure` and `compress` (off by default) in
                                 OMC_HOME/settings.json; the self-entry check
                                 knows the module name too.
  oh_my_context/serve.py         stdio only; its own initialize instructions;
                                 tools/list marks call/inspect/manifest/
                                 resolve_skills with _meta "anthropic/alwaysLoad";
                                 `call` takes only an original Claude tool name
                                 (mcp__...) or server plus tool; a server's own
                                 instructions come with its first call; a
                                 server's "timeout" is honoured for calls; the
                                 destructive-tool block is skipped only for a
                                 `call` that resolved to an exact route; upstream
                                 isError results and content blocks pass through;
                                 stdio requests run on their own threads and
                                 honour notifications/cancelled; the cold index
                                 reads the cache and fetches missing servers in
                                 parallel through the pool; routed servers'
                                 prompts and resources pass through; results are
                                 compressed only with `compress` set to smart.
  oh_my_context/native_tools.py  `call` and `inspect` accept original Claude
                                 tool names (resolve_claude_name); the `call`
                                 schema offers only the two call forms; inspect
                                 shows the instructions of a server that is
                                 already running and never starts one for them;
                                 kb_index takes a local path only; notices point
                                 to /oh-my-context-mod.
  oh_my_context/client.py        keeps a server's initialize instructions;
                                 upstream servers start without the launcher's
                                 PYTHONPATH/PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX/OMC_* variables
                                 and remote HTTP servers use the proxy
                                 environment (loopback stays direct); an expired
                                 HTTP session (404 with Mcp-Session-Id) is
                                 re-initialized and the request retried once; an
                                 HTTP error body that is not a JSON-RPC error
                                 object (an OAuth {"error": "..."}) raises
                                 HTTP_ERROR, and a 401 says to keep the server in
                                 direct_servers; a server that exited before the
                                 response deadline is reported as PROCESS_DIED,
                                 not RESPONSE_TIMEOUT (ported from upstream
                                 mcptoon commit 27dd0ddac).
  oh_my_context/skills.py        only the index the plugin builds and the BM25
                                 resolve over it; skills are indexed by their
                                 frontmatter name (the Skill tool's id).
  oh_my_context/cache.py         per-server files under OMC_HOME/cache only.
  oh_my_context/ccr.py           the store lives in OMC_HOME/ccr, never expires
                                 and keeps one session per gateway process.
  oh_my_context/compressor.py    used only by the gateway.
  oh_my_context/floodguard.py    blocks only (no soft cap), fixed limits.
  oh_my_context/headers.py       documentation only.
  oh_my_context/kb.py            local files only (no URL fetch).
  oh_my_context/plugin.py        only the SKILL.md frontmatter reader.
  oh_my_context/router.py        only the safety screens.
  oh_my_context/session_log.py   the log lives in OMC_HOME/sessions.
  oh_my_context/usage.py         only the call counter the `usage` tool reads;
                                 tokens are estimated as characters / 4.
